  "content": "# useSelectedDocument hook is auto-generated per document model\n\nFor each document model, the system generates a corresponding hook:\n\n- `Todo` model \u2192 `useSelectedTodoDocument`\n- `Invoice` model \u2192 `useSelectedInvoiceDocument`\n- `ServiceOffering` model \u2192 `useSelectedServiceOfferingDocument`\n\nThese hooks are generated inside the document-model package and are imported from its barrel (e.g. `import { useSelectedTodoDocument } from \"todo-app/document-models/todo\";`) \u2014 there is no `editors/hooks/` folder. They return `[document, dispatch]`. Never implement them manually \u2014 they follow a specific pattern that matches the document model's type system.\n\nSince [[editors use the modern React hooks pattern from reactor-browser]], these hooks are the standard entry point for all editor components.\n\n---\n\nTopics:\n- [[editor patterns]]\n- [[model-editor wiring]]\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
